# Due Diligence Module

> Validate acquisition readiness by verifying ownership, property data, documentation, commercial viability, and operational requirements before Title Review.

---

# Overview

The Due Diligence module is the operational quality control checkpoint within the mineral acquisition lifecycle.

After a Purchase & Sale Agreement (PSA) has been executed, every acquisition enters Due Diligence. During this stage, acquisition specialists verify ownership information, property records, lease data, operator details, legal descriptions, supporting documentation, and overall acquisition risk before forwarding the transaction to Title Review.

The module ensures that incomplete or high-risk acquisitions are identified early, reducing legal issues, unnecessary title costs, and delayed closings.

---

# Objectives

The Due Diligence module enables users to:

- Verify owner information
- Validate property information
- Review executed PSA
- Confirm lease and operator data
- Verify county records
- Review supporting documentation
- Identify acquisition risks
- Generate operational checklists
- Recommend Go / No-Go decisions
- Prepare transactions for Title Review

